**(A4)** The legal discount rate \( r: [0,1] \to [r_0, \infty) \) is continuous and strictly decreasing, with \( r(1) = r_0 \). Set \( \rho(L) := r(L)/r_0 \ge 1 \).

**(A5)** The carrying capacity \( K_{\max}: (0,\infty) \times [0,1] \to (0,\infty) \) is smooth, strictly decreasing in \( c \), and strictly increasing in \( L \).

### 2.3 Elementary Identities

